Z||000005||olympic||06-29-2000||01:38 AM||||   Those Grand Am Gt's are sweet.  While they're not super fast I really like the way they look.  The side profile kind of reminds me of a Mustang(no flames please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )  The wing, exhaust tips and front facia look really mean. I think that Pontiac is the only GM division left that has any styling talent.  The current Chevy styling sucks!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||frontal lobe||06-29-2000||02:25 PM||||Nice car!  Congratulations.  Cars have come a LONG way since I started buying them in the '70's.  You would have needed to buy a sports car back then for what performance and handling you get now in this car (at least the handling part).  This car may not have head-snapping acceleration, but it's certainly no pooch.  Faster than the 4-bangers in Accords, Camrys, Galants, 626's etc for about the same money (although those are fine cars, not bashing them).<P>And thanks GM for making a grown man get on his knees and beg:  would you PLEASE start putting 5-speed manuals with your v-6's?  GM makes some really nice v-6's that would go GREAT with a 5-speed.  ||||reg||1
